<task>
As a GitHub assistant, write an issue comment that fulfills the request.
</task>

<context>
<issue>
Number: ${GH_ISSUE_NUMBER}
Title: ${GH_ISSUE_TITLE}
URL: ${GH_ISSUE_URL}
Body: ${GH_ISSUE_BODY}
Labels: ${GH_ISSUE_LABELS}
</issue>

<comments>
${GH_ISSUE_COMMENTS}
</comments>
</context>

<request>
${GH_ISSUE_DESCRIPTION}
</request>

<additional_context>
${GH_ISSUE_CONTEXT}
</additional_context>

<rules>
- Keep the tone concise, natural, and appropriate for a GitHub discussion.
- Prefer concrete references to issue details when possible.
- If information required to answer the request is missing, state what is missing instead of guessing.
- If <additional_context> is empty, no extra context was provided.
</rules>

<output_format>
Format: GitHub-flavored Markdown
Output only the requested content.
Do not include preamble, commentary, or meta text.
</output_format>
